From: Pedro Maione <pedro.maione@9elements.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:28:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fansensor: do not exit when a presence GPIO cannot be set up

The PresenceGpio constructors throw std::runtime_error when the GPIO
named in a fan's Presence configuration does not exist or cannot be
requested, but createSensors() only catches std::system_error. A
misspelled PinName, or a line held by another consumer, terminates
fansensor and takes every fan PWM sensor down with it.

Catch std::runtime_error, which std::system_error derives from, so the
error is logged and the fan is created without presence detection.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/fan/FanMain.cpp |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
index d0d87eb..9210fd0 100644
--- a/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
+++ b/src/fan/FanMain.cpp
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <optional>
 #include <regex>
+#include <stdexcept>
 #include <string>
 #include <string_view>
 #include <system_error>
@@ -530,7 +531,7 @@ void createSensors(
                                 }
                                 presenceGpios[*pinName] = presenceGpio;
                             }
-                            catch (const std::system_error& e)
+                            catch (const std::runtime_error& e)
                             {
                                 lg2::error(
                                     "Failed to create GPIO monitor object for "
